What are Polymers for Wires and Cables?
Polymers for wires and cables represent specialized materials engineered for insulation, jacketing, and shielding applications in electrical infrastructure. These compounds - including PVC, polyethylene (PE), cross-linked polyethylene (XLPE), and halogen-free flame retardants - account for approximately 10% of total cable manufacturing costs. The industry is currently undergoing a significant transition toward sustainable alternatives while maintaining stringent performance requirements for power transmission and data communication networks.

